<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:37Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East live: Houthi attacks wound 13 civilians in southern Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ecb3663b3817f52320be343a5017fea39b0b1b2a3fda312f6fbfa0ffef71b59</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T03:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia--99d547e8fe8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">A series of attacks carried out by Yemen's Houthis using ballistic missiles and drones wounded 13 civilians in southern Saudi Arabia on Tuesday. Meanwhile the US Defence Department's inspector general revealed that the United States is facing a shortfall in ammunition as a result of its costly war in Iran. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy meetings in Texas at US's invitation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c347f3f2f3228520152e7bfa4c4c42fefec33a7ba2afcac9e62542babc10b735</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T02:44:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation--7120fef6df3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation" /><summary type="html">A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dae94502d9d53901e997fd8580e3744e25ff8e1f483f017583b40a120954fcb</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins--73bfd34fa579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump calls concerns over rogue AI a 'hoax' promoted by a ‘SICK conspiracy’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e87a97028e756f191cad529060257b8c675706b00c92fd025a80bd978100810</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:05:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-trump-calls-concerns-over-rogue-ai-a-hoax-promoted-by-a-sick-conspiracy--48ee873441f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-trump-calls-concerns-over-rogue-ai-a-hoax-promoted-by-a-sick-conspiracy" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Monday rejected warnings about the risks of artificial intelligence, calling concerns over rogue AI part of a “SICK conspiracy” as tech leaders urge greater safeguards. The clash comes as the rapidly advancing technology faces scrutiny over cybersecurity, jobs, data centres and its potential impact on national security.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Dangote refinery launches Africa’s biggest IPO for retail investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:132a3f19ad423ae45a8f8ff399650757b9cb1d404112a8449605d221301fb05e</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T00:05:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-dangote-refinery-launches-africa-biggest-ipo-for-retail-investors--a7186d02f0a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-dangote-refinery-launches-africa-biggest-ipo-for-retail-investors" /><summary type="html">Africa’s richest man Aliko Dangote on Monday launched an IPO for his $19 billion Nigerian oil refinery, seeking $1.6 billion from retail investors across the continent. The offering values Africa’s largest refinery at about $49 billion and has drawn both strong investor interest and concerns over its high valuation.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5239b62c0a9452e3dad8c7f936bd88468f8ade1d2a200eefce73dd28af74178c</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes--596ec22eafa5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Macklemore dropped from Ed Sheeran US tour after pro-Palestinian remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3de5fa25d10774fb30991ca6b64421b4515b7e6d4343f999852b53683be42183</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks--73709c875802.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks" /><summary type="html">American rapper Macklemore announced on Monday that he was dropped from Ed Sheeran’s US stadium tour after saying "Free Palestine" during a September 4 concert in New Jersey. The Grammy winner’s removal follows pressure from venue owners, including New England Patriots owner Robert Kraft, over his criticism of Israel’s actions in Gaza.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Space Force confirms weapons deployed in space for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6b08d8a5557f5799c018f51a0e7e54b9971afcbbd686cc1c9ebc4cd6615b2ec</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time--b77423806d11.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">The US Space Force has confirmed for the first time that Washington has weapons deployed in orbit, as the United States, China and Russia expand military capabilities in space. The disclosure highlights a growing focus on controlling the space domain and protecting satellites vital to military communications, surveillance and navigation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Bob Mackie, fashion designer for the stars, dies at 87</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c11d9e5d77d62cb45cd4c0e39f7d4f22538bef40e99d19bdd4c8141c5426936</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:40:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/bob-mackie-fashion-designer-for-the-stars-dies-at-87--8a99547beeb1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/bob-mackie-fashion-designer-for-the-stars-dies-at-87" /><summary type="html">⁠Hollywood designer ⁠Bob Mackie, ​known for making stars such as Cher and ​Elton John sparkle, died on Monday at 87, according to a post on his official Instagram account. His career ​spanned ‌five decades and included ⁠designing a Barbie doll clothes collection. FRANCE 24's Camille Knight has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rights group accuses Israel of dismantling 'Palestinian existence' in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ab6e944dbef5e581a97e4ad892ceba7e611939edd6be0e964da1b7f9941cc08</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:04:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:26:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank--8f7b227ed62c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli rights group B'Tselem said Monday that Israeli actions in the occupied West Bank form part of a greater project designed to make it impossible for Palestinians to exist together as a people. In a report titled "The Elimination Project", the group alleged five connected Israeli tactics and policies in the West Bank: "violence, ethnic cleansing, movement restrictions, economic strangulation, social and political destruction". FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fact-checking videos claiming to show Houthi rebel attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbdd743d6098dfb7484df34d8a3d4049cda1d4f660b8b63c02bea8aa7720bd20</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1--01e7b543b98c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1" /><summary type="html">A video claiming to show Houthi rebels ambushing Saudi-backed mercenaries has racked up major views on X. But the FRANCE 24 Observers found it is actually footage of 2024 Houthi military drills. The clip was edited with football commentary and blurred flags, which originally show Israel, the UK and US, not Saudi Arabia. Other viral videos falsely linked to Houthi attacks on a Saudi Aramco refinery were also traced to unrelated fires in Texas and Russia. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'The very existence of LGBTQI people is seen as obscene', Turkish activist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c35464ac2878781ecb688a092984a298601a51d096c24133af034d21f2fa499</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:02:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says--7e48c4e3384e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday swooped on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan lashing it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's Dangote refinery kicks off blockbuster IPO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9f65b71708dfbfcafdacb610ad2368056fc34f2ac9b7aa56e69cc1727d10ffa</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T20:46:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260914-nigeria-s-dangote-refinery-kicks-off-blockbuster-ipo--71a681865ade.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260914-nigeria-s-dangote-refinery-kicks-off-blockbuster-ipo" /><summary type="html">Nigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote launched the biggest-ever share sale on the African continent, listing 4.1 billion shares in his Lagos refinery on the stock exchange.  He framed it as a "people's IPO" to give all Nigerians a chance to share the plant's wealth potentials. Trading is expected to start in November. Meanwhile, global oil prices continued to advance as attacks by Yemen's Houthi rebels forced Saudi Arabia to shut down its East-West oil pipeline.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian oil refinery Dangote aims to raise 1.6 billion dollars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:682d7675dd5e92444ca5f2178dbbb8639343e10827d86efc737ee4c4ad39b3af</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T20:31:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigerian-oil-refinery-dangote-aims-to-raise-1-6-billion-dollars--8328c51224d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigerian-oil-refinery-dangote-aims-to-raise-1-6-billion-dollars" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Nigeria's Dangote refinery opens itself to public ownership with plans to raise 1.6 billion dollars from retail investors across the continent. Also, President Felix Tshisekedi calls on the National Service to clean up the streets of Kinshasa. And with a month and a half to go until the Youth Olympic Games begin, the Olympic flame begins its tour of Senegal, the tournament's host country.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7845676a90d406ac2ec661b4838c846021ee278c88b8de9a71f3e156757d8b08</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:54:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas--85ad9b6b4b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas" /><summary type="html">Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'Axis of Iranian centrality' remains "one of more destabilising forces in the region", expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5746158ae67577dcd6adba05ef06096d721bdb8eb9c9950cd8ee90d1b43a7fff</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:46:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says--4aee9c340b4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/axis-of-iranian-centrality-remains-one-of-more-destabilising-forces-in-the-region-expert-says" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis launched a fresh barrage of missile and drone attacks on Saudi military targets on Monday, as Iran denied any involvement in the country's revived civil war. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Dr H. A. Hellyer, Senior Fellow in Geopolitics, International Security, and Middle East Studies at the Royal United Services Institute, says that Iran and its non-state proxies "remain to be one of the more destabilising forces in the region alongside the Israeli project of regional paramountcy".</summary></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to boost Arctic role to tackle Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d669862f08c137560e6c5d7fa4c1f7dbf7e860631260773967e10639bb8f966</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:06:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat--d1df20e91748.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/leaders-urge-eu-to-boost-arctic-role-to-tackle-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries meeting in Finland on Monday urged the European Union to beef up its presence in the Arctic, a geopolitical battleground caught between Russia and US President Donald Trump. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Where is the kill switch? AI doomsday warnings trigger calls to regulate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd427df7b6d1e9093d4c5f0d54587ccbf318cf245ea1c8ce569b96beacc88249</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:22:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260914-where-is-the-kill-switch-ai-doomsday-warnings-trigger-calls-to-regulate--00227f34643a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260914-where-is-the-kill-switch-ai-doomsday-warnings-trigger-calls-to-regulate" /><summary type="html">Talk about doomsday scrolling. In the past week, our timelines have been alight with dark predictions of our imminent demise, including the one by a Silicon Valley engineer who puts a number on the chances of artificial intelligence wiping out humanity. Better than 10-percent. Triggering the wave of panic, the recent breach of the machine-learning programmers' site Hugging Face by AI machines who banded together to keep their nefarious deeds secret from their human overlords. Can machines actually destroy the planet on their own? In the age of technology, does problem solving always override safety?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Leaders urge EU to expand Arctic presence amid Russia 'threat'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7427fabc12478ce4966a4a289a43da6140c4fdc0c3f468c694d6ff53f4a00ae2</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:41:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat--e35c64118e5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-leaders-urge-eu-to-expand-arctic-presence-amid-russia-threat" /><summary type="html">Twelve European countries on Monday called for the European Union to step up its presence in the Arctic, as melting ice opens new maritime routes while growing tensions with Russia and the United States increasingly put the region in the geopolitical spotlight.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>French candidates race to claim the cost-of-living issue ahead of 2027 vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11f9edc642ed43a299bae589988fa0714959db204a969ab94d367c0d06ed279e</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T16:53:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260914-french-candidates-race-to-claim-the-cost-of-living-issue-ahead-of-2027-vote--8cd1ecf11dca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260914-french-candidates-race-to-claim-the-cost-of-living-issue-ahead-of-2027-vote" /><summary type="html">A new Ipsos survey reveals a country gripped by pessimism, with soaring prices the top worry for French voters ahead of the April 2027 presidential election. Candidates from far-right leader Marine Le Pen, to the far-left's Jean-Luc Mélenchon are racing to make the cost of living the defining issue of their campaigns.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Police arrested at least 63 people in anti-LGBT+ crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a767dc29394b636341351a108a2cbf3fc7d12bdce3df08c5b211af5af073864f</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:43:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-turkey-police-arrested-at-least-63-people-in-anti-lgbt-crackdown--09977501beea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-turkey-police-arrested-at-least-63-people-in-anti-lgbt-crackdown" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities on Sunday launched raids on gay bars, nightclubs, LGBTQ association offices and activists' homes in a sweeping crackdown in several cities as part of the government's "My Family is Safe" operations, Turkey's justice minister said.
 
More than 60 people were arrested, according to the state news agency, in raids condemned by human rights groups.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poll puts France's Le Pen in lead as presidential campaign kicks off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:198b450351af3ca46a24854412410d0d03077f15de0c2b1cb5dd6891a5d0e0ae</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:59:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-polls-put-france-s-le-pen-in-lead-as-presidential-campaign-kicks-off--0437140198a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-polls-put-france-s-le-pen-in-lead-as-presidential-campaign-kicks-off" /><summary type="html">France's far-right veteran candidate Marine Le Pen looks set to lead in the first round of elections next year, as the country's increasingly disillusioned voters seek real change, a poll of more than 13,000 voters has suggested.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian strike on train "terror knocking on EU's door'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f1442590b58485dd6e1b003de953735b4cdcffc4a5a68cb2b6690a49ddfa43d</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:57:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russian-strike-on-train-terror-knocking-on-eu-s-door--898e58711366.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-russian-strike-on-train-terror-knocking-on-eu-s-door" /><summary type="html">The Kremlin said on Monday it would keep striking targets across the "whole" of Ukraine, when asked about a rare drone attack on the Polish border that has rattled Warsaw and its European allies. NATO-member Poland said on Sunday that Russia had hit a railway locomotive inside Ukraine, about two kilometres (one mile) from their shared border, just days after Kyiv said it had hit a crossing at its border with Moldova.</summary></entry></feed>
